Independently inspect executable code for each requested {locus, name} feature.
Do not trust comments, identifiers, requested edits, or prior_actions as proof.
Follow the actual data flow at that locus. A mechanism elsewhere does not count.
Use only INPUT_JSON.source_files, available at INPUT_JSON.source_dir/<file key>.
This read-only snapshot is authoritative. Never scan sharedwork, repositories,
or prior artifacts. Report unknown if these sources cannot establish presence
or absence.

Return {"checks": [{"feature": {"locus": "...", "name": "..."},
"status": "present|absent|unknown", "reason": "Brief source-based explanation.",
"evidence": [{"path": "source_files key", "start": 1, "end": 1}]}]}.
Include exactly one check per feature. Present AND absent require a reason and
source evidence: for absence, inspect the whole locus and relevant callees,
cite decisive ranges, and explain why they exclude the mechanism at that locus.
Missing definitions mean unknown.
Use one-based inclusive line ranges, at most {{ citation_limit }} citations per
feature and {{ line_limit }} lines per citation. Cite source_files keys, not absolute
paths. Omit quote: the verifier restores exact source text and hashes locally.
Choose minimal decisive ranges and keep
each reason to one or two sentences. Do not copy source into intermediate
evidence catalogs, edit files, or omit unresolved checks. Return only the JSON.
